# TINA-MANAGED CONTENT. Same principle as tokens.css above: the tool that writes
# the file owns its formatting, and Prettier is not that tool.
#
# Every collection in `tina/config.ts` writes here (`venues`, `leagues`,
# `memberships`, `rates`, `menu`, `testimonials`, `faq` as json; `pages` as md).
# Tina and Prettier disagree about both of its formats, in opposite directions:
# Tina writes arrays expanded one-item-per-line and Prettier collapses them onto
# one line, while Tina writes an FAQ entry as a single line and Prettier expands
# it. So `npm run format` rewrote content nobody had edited, and the client's
# next save in the CMS reverted it — permanent churn between two tools that both
# believe they own the file. Three separate agents had to unpick that by hand
# before committing (FW-4023).
#
# Scoped to the two content FORMATS rather than the whole directory on purpose:
# `src/content/config.ts` is hand-written Zod schema, it is code, and
# eslint-plugin-prettier enforces Prettier on it through `npm run lint`.
# Ignoring the directory wholesale would silently switch that off.
src/content/**/*.json
src/content/**/*.md
